config BR2_PACKAGE_SDROXIDE
	bool "sdroxide"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_RUSTC_TARGET_ARCH_SUPPORTS
	select BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_RUSTC
	select BR2_PACKAGE_ALSA_LIB
	select BR2_PACKAGE_RUST_WASM
	select BR2_PACKAGE_STUNNEL
	help
	  SDRoxide (https://github.com/dividebysandwich/sdroxide), built
	  headless (native GUI dropped -- see 0001-drop-native-gui-server-only)
	  for `sdroxide --server`: drives this board's own Pluto-compatible
	  IIOD locally and serves TCI/OpenHPSDR/rigctld plus a WebSocket API
	  for a browser client (crates/sdroxide-web, built here too -- see
	  sdroxide.mk). The server binary is large (tens of MB) -- it embeds
	  several neural-net models (CW decode, noise reduction, the
	  FreeDV/RADE vocoder) that ship with upstream regardless of which
	  radio backend is used -- so neither it nor the web client's ~35MB
	  wasm bundle goes into the ramdisk rootfs; both ship on the SD
	  card's FAT boot partition instead (see postimage-sd.sh /
	  S65sdroxide). Only meaningful on an SD-booting board.

	  sdroxide-server has no TLS of its own, and browsers withhold Web
	  Audio (microphone / audio playback) outside a secure context. A
	  stunnel front end (S45sdroxide-tls-cert, stunnel-sdroxide.conf)
	  wraps it in TLS with a throwaway self-signed cert on port 4951,
	  alongside the plain HTTP port 4950.
